equirements\nDecisions + Conditions\nTuition + Fees\nTuition Types\nFees\nBudget Calculator\nVisiting + Incoming Exchange\nWestern Deans and CAGS Mobility Agreements\nGraduate Visiting Research Student\nNon-degree Student\nAwards + Funding\nInternal + Donor Funded Awards\nDonor Stories\nTRI-Agency & Government Awards\nThesis Dissertation Awards + Convocation Medals\nExternal + Additional Awards\nRoles + Responsibilities\nPayments + Policies\nAward Application Resources\nGraduate Students\nGetting Started\nUnderstanding Your Role\nStudent Status\nStudent Responsibilities\nGraduate Student Handbook\nManaging Your Program\nDates + Deadlines\nFees\nEnrollment\nAcademic Supervision\nConflict of Interest + Graduate Studies\nGrading + Academic Progress\nGenerative + Agentic Artificial Intelligence Use\nTransfers\nWithdraw\nWithdrawals under Extenuating Circumstances\nApply for WE\nReturning to Studies\nAppeals\nForms\nApply for WE\nCompleting + Graduation\nCompletion Option Guidelines\nMaster's Degree\nThesis\nOral Examination\nDoctoral Degree\nThesis\nOral Examination\nEarly Completion Refund\nCredential Confirmation\nConvocation\nLife + Community\nCommunity Guide\nIndigenous Graduate Students\nInternational Graduate Students\nSucceed in English\nProfessional Development\nYour Career Compass\nRSVP for Session: Your Career Compass (YCC) Retreat\nJobs + Volunteering\nEmployment Type\nJob Posting Form\nPeople + Research\nGrad Student Profiles\nSubmit Your Profile\nParticipate in Grad Student Research\nSubmission Form\nNews + Events\nNews\nEvents\n3 Minute Thesis\nPresident's Dream Colloquium\nSubmit Your Event/Activity\nFaculty + Staff\nSupervisor + Reviewer Resources\nExternal Examiners\nIndividualized Interdisciplinary Studies in Graduate Studies\nApply\nPrograms\nCurrent Students\nAwards + Funding\nResearch + Events\nSupervisor's Corner\nApplying\nReady to start your graduate student experience at Simon Fraser University?\nThere is no general admission at the graduate level at SFU, as admission is specific to each program. You may apply to as many programs as you wish within an application period.\nSimon Fraser University operates on a trimester system. The Fall term is from September through December, the Spring term is from January through April, and the Summer term is from May through August.\nDecisions for fall admissions are announced starting in February and continue through summer. Each program has a different review period that follows its admission deadline. For questions about decisions and offers of financial support, contact your program directly.\nExplore Graduate Programs\nAdmission is specific to each program; you must apply to your program(s) of interest. Visit the program or department website for more information on that program and admission deadlines. After comparing programs, if you still have questions, reach out to the program through the contact information listed on the program website.\nExplore list of graduate programs\nReview Admission Requirements\nEven if you meet the minimum University requirements for admission you are not assured admission into any graduate program. Most graduate programs have program-specific admission requirements in addition to the minimum which can be found on their program website.\nReview requirements\nOrder/Prepare Application Materials\nPrepare your application information and supporting documents. Individual graduate programs will require different components and submissions. We recommend contacting potential supervisors (if required) and your referees well in advance of starting the admission application.\nEnglish language test scores, where required, are sent to us electronically, directly from the testing agency. We encourage you to release your results as early as possible, as they can take approximately 4 weeks to process onto your application.\nLearn about test scores\nApply Online\nThe online application has 3 steps and we advise you work ahead of your program deadline:\nStart and submit the application form\nCan take approximately 45 minutes. Includes identification, academic history etc.\nYou can only submit your form before the application deadline.\nPay the non-refundable application fee\nSubmit the payment 5\u20137 days prior to the final deadline to allow for processing time.\nApplication Fees are $112 for applicants with Canadian transcripts, $160 for applicants with international transcripts.\nChecklist (upload supporting documentation)\nRequired documents depend on the program and may include transcripts, curriculum vitae, research proposal etc. Once you submit your form and application fee, you can immediately proceed to invite references and upload documents within your portal. All required supporting documentation and references need to be completed by your program's deadline (the deadlines for documents and references are set by each program).\nApply Online\nComplete the online application\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nAbout\nApply\nAwards + Funding\nGraduate Students\nLife + Community\nContact us\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nMaggie Benston Centre 1100\nSimon Fraser University\n8888 University Drive\nBurnaby, B.C.\nCanada V5A 1S6\nSafety & Risk\nSFU Maps & Directions\nSFU Admissions\nRoad Report\nGive to SFU\nEmergency Information\nA-Z Directory\nSimon Fraser University respectfully acknowledges the x\u02b7m\u0259\u03b8k\u02b7\u0259y\u0313\u0259m (Musqueam), S\u1e35wx\u0331w\u00fa7mesh \u00daxwumixw (Squamish), s\u0259lilw\u0259ta\u026c (Tsleil-Waututh), q\u0313\u00edc\u0313\u0259y\u0313 (Katzie), k\u02b7ik\u02b7\u0259\u019b\u0313\u0259m (Kwikwetlem), Qayqayt, Kwantlen, Semiahmoo and Tsawwassen peoples on whose unceded traditional territories our three campuses reside.\nTerms & ConditionsPrivacy policy\u00a9 Simon Fraser University\nAbout\nOverview\nContact Us\nDean's Welcome\nGraduate Studies Awards for Excellence\nOverview\nGraduate Supervision\nGraduate Leadership\nGraduate Service\nStrategic Plan & Priorities\n